## Context and authority

Filed from replicator (post-0003) at the author's request, 2026-11-27. The
author read the two frozen pilot reports
(`replications/weschle2024politicians/report/weschle2024politicians-report.pdf`,
`replications/atanasov2024taste/report/main.pdf`) and gave 24 remarks
(W1-W17 on Weschle, A1-A7 on Atanasov). The author ruled the dispatch below.
Paper-specific points stay in replicator; the reports are frozen and are not
edited. Weschle ran at harness `04d8cf2`, before the identification review
existed; Atanasov at `2360e75`. Overlap to check: 1572-1579 (data audit,
asserted checks, Stata caveats, calibration split, private packages,
unprinted estimates). Priority: report-style items before the Toulouse
Games (8 Dec 2026), because reports go to teammates.

## SKILL.md rules (one binding line each)

| Rule | Remarks |
|---|---|
| Every discrepancy says what it compares: an internal inconsistency of the article (text vs its own table) or a reproduction difference (printed vs recomputed) | W7 |
| Every discrepancy is qualified (typo or swapped labels, rounding, Monte Carlo noise tested against its Monte Carlo SE, substantive unresolved); negligibility is computed, not asserted. Identical software, RNG and seed should give zero Monte Carlo difference; a difference then needs a cause | W8, W14, A2 |
| A statistic with no author code that is trivial to recompute from the analysis data gets a separate status (e.g. `recomputed`), counted apart from author-code matches; `not_run` only with a stated reason. The analysis-code-provided row still records the missing code | A6 |
| assess flags data-acquisition code (scraper, API calls, downloads); the report states whether acquisition was replayed; a temporal extension is a direct replication, proposed with cost and terms-of-use limits, never run unsigned (outward act) | A5 |
| probe proposes for the main result at least one check outside the paper's statistical frame: model-independent (permutation/randomization inference, rank or distribution tests), a different design on the same data (within-unit comparisons, exact matching), or a derived implication of the same hypothesis. Signing rules unchanged; the report separates in-frame and out-of-frame checks | A7 |
| When a check overturns a key result, the report discusses the model-selection criteria (estimand, count outcome and zeros, field practice) and states the specification-search question explicitly, on verifiable facts (justification in the paper, pre-registration, field norm), without imputing intent | W13 |
| Identification review asks two separate questions: is the estimation faithful to the causal graph (internal), and is the graph credible against other studies and common sense (scientific). Strong model plus targeted, verified checks; then stop and offer, with a cost, before any deep literature search or saturation | A4 |
| The run records AI Disclosure data as it goes (see the report-style reference) | W16 |

## References (procedure and format)

| Reference | Content | Remarks |
|---|---|---|
| Report style (new reference or template section) | Caption on every table and figure; report tables numbered R1, R2 (`\renewcommand{\thetable}{R\arabic{table}}`), article tables always cited as "article Table n"; the I4R reproducibility table captioned with the name I4R/Brodeur uses; no template-internal phrase ("in the template") without context; the substantive effect restated in plain words before each numeric comparison | W1, W2, W4, W6, A1, W12 |
| Report style | I4R table: "?" in the cells the assessor hesitates between, never a blank row. The checklist row "Computational requirements: libraries/packages, running time" is verbatim in all three I4R templates: keep it, add below a row marked as an addition, "Provides a ready-to-run environment (container image or lockfile)", and say in the text whether package versions are listed | W3, W5 |
| Report style | Robustness section: keep the I4R heading "Robustness Reproduction" and open with one sentence defining it (same data, alternative analytical decisions; not an extension); checks excluded because the paper or SI already reports them are said to be reproduced in the reproduction section, cross-referenced by label; counts of signed, run and not-run checks, each not-run with its reason | W9, W10, W11 |
| Report style | Signature "Auto-generated by <model>, guided by <user>"; AI Disclosure with the project repository and commit, the harness repository and commit, and per role (MOE, team leads, coders, reviewers) the model, number of calls and share of work | W16 |
| rules.md or a discrepancy reference | Pre-specified negligibility diagnostic reported beside the strict three-digit verdict (the strict verdict and tolerance unchanged): difference as a fraction of the SE with an equivalence margin, difference against the Monte Carlo SE for simulated quantities, count at the second digit | W14, W8 |
| identification-review.md | Causal graph in the body at the start of the section, caption stating claim and estimand; a threats table (path, status, evidence, what would rule it out) instead of prose; verdict on the scale; a section on the credibility of the graph itself; the stop-and-offer point before deep search | A3, A4 |
| robustness-menus.md | A category "verify the claim by a model-independent method", with sources | A7 |

## Out of scope here

Paper-specific findings (Weschle Monte Carlo difference under identical R and
seed, the Poisson discussion, Atanasov swapped values and the 3,382 vs 3,852
count, the scraper not replayed) stay in replicator's journal. A replicator
remote is a replicator decision.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Receiving Imagine records facts, overlap with 1572-1579, ownership and
  standing rulings, and disposes of each row above.
- [ ] Report-style rows are implemented or explicitly deferred before
  2026-12-08.
